C*******************************************************************************
C                         Water Supply Requirement 
C
C   The following lists the water supply requirement column pointers for each finite  
C   element and ponded crop combination.  
C
C   IE    ;  Element ID (Enter 0 if following values are to be used for all element
C              and ponded crop combinations)
C   ICAW  ;  Water supply requirement - this number corresponds to the appropriate  
C              data column in the agricultural water supply requirement data 
C              file (AGWDFL) listed in the Root Zone Parameters Data File. List for  
C              each ponded crop (1 to NRICE + NREFUGE).
C              * Enter 0 if water supply requirement will be computed internally.
C              * List the column pointers in the same order as the crop 
C                codes (CCODE) are listed above; first for rice categories, 
C                then for refuge categories
C
C--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C   IE  ICAW_RI_FL  ICAW_RI_NFL  ICAW_RI_NDC  ICAW_RF_SL  ICAW_RF_PR
C--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     0     0            0            0            0            0
C*******************************************************************************
C                         Irrigation Periods 
C
C   The following lists the irrigation period column pointers for each   
C   finite element and ponded crop combinations.
C
C   IE    ;  Element ID (Enter 0 if following values are to be used for all element
C              and ponded crop combinations)
C   ICIP  ;  Irrigation period - this number corresponds to the appropriate data 
C              column in the irrigation period data file (IPFL) listed in the Root 
C              Zone Parameters Data File. List for each ponded crop  
C              (1 to NRICE + NREFUGE).
C              * List the column pointers in the same order as the crop 
C                codes (CCODE) are listed above; first for rice categories, 
C                then for refuge categories
